    <bpmn:process id="W_W5483" name="W5483. EV &amp; Alt-Fuel Fleet Safety — High-Voltage, Battery Fire &amp; DOLE-OSH Program" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: EV/alt-fuel vehicles in service; safety-program establishment; any HV/thermal/fire event
Frequency: Continuous program; per event
Volume: Whole green fleet + charging infrastructure + drivers/technicians/first-responders
Owner: HSE Manager (VS-24)
Participants: Fleet (VS-06), Facilities (VS-138), Maintenance (W5480), Drivers/technicians, Fire/BFP, emergency responders
Source: workflow W5483 — EV &amp; Alt-Fuel Fleet Safety — High-Voltage, Battery Fire &amp; DOLE-OSH Program</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5483_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5483_Lane1" name="HSE Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5483_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5483_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5483_Lane2" name="HSE">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5483_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5483_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5483_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5483_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5483_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5483_Start4" name="EV/alt-fuel vehicles in service; safety-program establishment; any HV/thermal/fire event">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5483_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5483_Task5" name="Establish the EV/alt-fuel fleet safety program under DOLE-OSH (RA 11058) and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Establish the EV/alt-fuel fleet safety program under DOLE-OSH (RA 11058) and BFP Fire Code: HV-work permits, LOTO/energy-isolation for HV systems, battery-fire response, and first-responder protocols.
Responsible (R): HSE Manager / Fleet
Accountable (A): COO (HSE Lead)
Duration: per program</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5483_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5483_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5483_Task6" name="Site the charging/alt-fuel infrastructure with BFP-compliant separation…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Site the charging/alt-fuel infrastructure with BFP-compliant separation, fire-detection/suppression appropriate to lithium-battery fires (not water), ventilation, and emergency shut-off (links W5468).
Responsible (R): HSE / Facilities / BFP
Accountable (A): COO (HSE Lead)
Duration: per site</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5483_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5483_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5483_Task7" name="Train drivers, technicians, and first-responders (links W5484) on HV safety…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Train drivers, technicians, and first-responders (links W5484) on HV safety, battery-fire response, and towing/recovery (W5480); maintain competency records.
Responsible (R): HSE / L&amp;D
Accountable (A): COO (HSE Lead)
Duration: per role</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5483_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5483_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5483_Task8" name="Investigate every HV/thermal/fire event to root cause (links VS-24 incident…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Investigate every HV/thermal/fire event to root cause (links VS-24 incident investigation), with corrective/preventive action; report serious incidents to DOLE/BFP per OSH/Fire-Code requirements.
Responsible (R): HSE
Accountable (A): COO (HSE Lead)
Duration: per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5483_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5483_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5483_Task9" name="Maintain emergency-response readiness (drills, equipment, mutual-aid with…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Maintain emergency-response readiness (drills, equipment, mutual-aid with BFP/LGU) and feed systemic issues into the recall path and the OEM/battery vendor (W5467/W5480).
Responsible (R): HSE / Fleet
Accountable (A): COO (HSE Lead)
Duration: ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5483_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5483_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5483_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5483_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-808 (ensure controlled execution — Green Fleet Performance, Compliance, Safety &amp; Analytics (PA-192.3).) | - operational: HV-work-permit/LOTO mandatory; lithium-fire-appropriate suppression; qualified-only HV work; reportable-incident DOLE/BFP notification.
Owner: HSE Manager (VS-24)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
