    <bpmn:process id="W_W5487" name="W5487. EV Battery Second-Life, End-of-Life Recycling &amp; RA 11898 EPR Linkage" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Battery end-of-first-life (degradation threshold W5475); vehicle end-of-life
Frequency: Per battery/vehicle retirement; scales with fleet conversion
Volume: Per retired EV battery / vehicle over the program life
Owner: Fleet Maintenance Manager (VS-06.2)
Participants: ESG (VS-25/VS-179), OEM/battery recycler, HSE (VS-24), Legal (VS-100), DENR-accredited TSD
Source: workflow W5487 — EV Battery Second-Life, End-of-Life Recycling &amp; RA 11898 EPR Linkage</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5487_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5487_Lane1" name="Fleet Maintenance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5487_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5487_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5487_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5487_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5487_Lane2" name="Fleet Maintenance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5487_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5487_Lane3" name="ESG">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5487_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5487_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5487_Start5" name="Battery end-of-first-life (degradation threshold W5475); vehicle end-of-life">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5487_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5487_Task6" name="At the degradation threshold (W5475), decide per battery: second-life reuse…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: At the degradation threshold (W5475), decide per battery: second-life reuse (stationary storage at a BuildRight site — links VS-108), refurbishment, or end-of-life recycling, based on SoH and economics.
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance / ESG
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: per battery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5487_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5487_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5487_Task7" name="For second-life, qualify the application (stationary storage capacity, BMS…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: For second-life, qualify the application (stationary storage capacity, BMS re-commissioning, safety), integrate with the solar/storage program (VS-108), and account for the residual value.
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance / Solar O&amp;M
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5487_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5487_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5487_Task8" name="For end-of-life, route to an OEM take-back program or a DENR-accredited…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: For end-of-life, route to an OEM take-back program or a DENR-accredited hazardous-waste transporter/TSD (RA 6969) and recycler capable of lithium-battery processing (links VS-187/VS-114).
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance / HSE
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: per battery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5487_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5487_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5487_Task9" name="Maintain battery traceability/passport (chemistry, SoH history, disposition…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Maintain battery traceability/passport (chemistry, SoH history, disposition, chain-of-custody to recycler) for ESG/EPR evidence and warranty (W5467/W5475).
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance Analyst
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5487_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5487_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5487_Task10" name="Align with RA 11898 (EPR Act) obligations on e-waste/extended producer…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Align with RA 11898 (EPR Act) obligations on e-waste/extended producer responsibility (links VS-179) and report battery diversion/recycling in ESG disclosure (VS-25).
Responsible (R): ESG / Fleet Maintenance
Accountable (A): Fleet Maintenance Manager
Duration: annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5487_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5487_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5487_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5487_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-808 (ensure controlled execution — Green Fleet Performance, Compliance, Safety &amp; Analytics (PA-192.3).) | - operational: DENR-accredited TSD/RA 6969 manifest with traceability/EPR evidence and recycler/TSD TPRM; documented disposition decision framework; chain-of-custody mandatory.
Owner: Fleet Maintenance Manager (VS-06.2)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5487_Assoc13" sourceRef="W5487_Annotation12" targetRef="W5487_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5487_Flow14" sourceRef="W5487_Start5" targetRef="W5487_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5487_Flow15" sourceRef="W5487_Task6" targetRef="W5487_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5487_Flow16" sourceRef="W5487_Task7" targetRef="W5487_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5487_Flow17" sourceRef="W5487_Task8" targetRef="W5487_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5487_Flow18" sourceRef="W5487_Task9" targetRef="W5487_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5487_Flow19" sourceRef="W5487_Task10" targetRef="W5487_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
