        <bpmn:outgoing>W5488_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5488_Task6" name="Maintain the green-fleet performance dashboard: tCO₂e vs target (W5481), kWh/km…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Maintain the green-fleet performance dashboard: tCO₂e vs target (W5481), kWh/km &amp; L/100km, eco-driving scores (W5476), charger uptime (W5474), fallback-usage (W5477), renewable-share (W5479), and cost/run vs TCO case (W5469).
Responsible (R): Fleet Analyst
Accountable (A): Fleet Analytics &amp; CI Lead
Duration: monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5488_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5488_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5488_Task7" name="Track benefit-realization vs the ex-ante business case (W5471): emissions…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Track benefit-realization vs the ex-ante business case (W5471): emissions reduction, energy/fuel cost savings, maintenance savings, and incentive realization; investigate variances.
Responsible (R): Fleet Analyst / Finance
Accountable (A): Fleet Analytics &amp; CI Lead
Duration: quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5488_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5488_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5488_Task8" name="Identify under-performing vehicles/lanes/sites/drivers and run root-cause…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Identify under-performing vehicles/lanes/sites/drivers and run root-cause (OpEx/VS-133): e.g., a site with high fallback-usage, a vehicle with abnormal degradation, a charger with low uptime.
Responsible (R): Fleet Analyst / OpEx
Accountable (A): Fleet Analytics &amp; CI Lead
Duration: per finding</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5488_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5488_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5488_Task9" name="Drive continuous improvement (links VS-133): route/charging-schedule tweaks…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Drive continuous improvement (links VS-133): route/charging-schedule tweaks, driver coaching, infrastructure additions, procurement-spec updates (W5467), and contract-clause refinement (W5485).
Responsible (R): Fleet Ops / Fleet Analytics
Accountable (A): Fleet Analytics &amp; CI Lead
Duration: per cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5488_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5488_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5488_Task10" name="Report program performance into the ESG/decarbonization governance (VS-25/VS-36…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Report program performance into the ESG/decarbonization governance (VS-25/VS-36 board) and feed the annual strategy refresh (W5465) and capital governance (W5471).
Responsible (R): Fleet Analytics / ESG
Accountable (A): Head of Supply Chain &amp; Logistics
Duration: annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5488_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5488_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5488_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5488_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-808 (ensure controlled execution — Green Fleet Performance, Compliance, Safety &amp; Analytics (PA-192.3).) | - operational: documented top-KPI set; exception-based review cadence.
Owner: Fleet Analytics &amp; Continuous Improvement Lead (VS-133/VS-06)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
